      309.36,
      366.72,
      545.04,
      375.6
     ],
     "text": "follow-up morphological and agronomic comparison involv-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.36,
      377.76,
      545.76,
      386.4
     ],
     "text": "ing 128 varieties, it showed a desirable combination of"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.36,
      388.8,
      545.04,
      397.44
     ],
     "text": "attributes for a pasture grass in central and southern"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.12,
      399.84,
      355.68,
      408.24
     ],
     "text": "Queensland."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Origin\n\u2018Medway\u2019 was initially selected from six B. pertusa varieties\non the basis of leafiness, robustness and flowering time. In a\nfollow-up morphological and agronomic comparison involv-\ning 128 varieties, it showed a desirable combination of\nattributes for a pasture grass in central and southern\nQueensland.",
